{
  "_about": "`attitude`: \"aggressive\" enemies attack anyone who comes within `detection`; \"passive\" ones (yellow names, like the wild boar) mind their own business until struck. An enemy with `dummy: true` (the training dummy) never moves, attacks or dies: its health fills again when it reaches zero or after a few seconds out of combat. Enemy types: stats, behaviour and what they drop. Where they stand is in world.json (enemySpawns). `type` (fodder, pack_beast, normal, skirmisher, armoured, elite, heavy, boss) and `level` work out health, damage, attackInterval, armour (or `armourClass`: none, light, armoured, heavy), an elite's special and an aimed shot (src/data/scaling.js); a number stated here wins. `respawn`: seconds after a kill before that spawn point brings the enemy back (0 = never, for bosses and story enemies). `skin`: the loot table a beast's body yields when skinned (with Skinning and a knife); the rank needed comes from its level (src/systems/loot.js skinRank).",
